The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/core/core-10-occupancy-gains.md`.

**Key findings summary:**

| Severity | Finding |
|----------|---------|
| **High** | HPXML-embedded occupancy weekday/weekend schedule fractions are parsed and stored in the Occupancy spec but **never used** to generate the occupancy timeseries — `schedule_resolve.rs:404` silently drops `ScheduleCategory::Occupancy` |
| **Medium** | Occupancy gain constants (66 W sensible, 51.2 W latent) derive from OCHRE's 400 BTU/h convention, not ASHRAE 55 (~70/45 W); no metabolic rate scaling for sleeping vs active states |
| **Medium** | No fallback from `NumberofBedrooms` to occupant count when HPXML `NumberofResidents` is absent |
| **Low** | Default schedule has identical weekday/weekend fractions (per standard), fractional occupancy is correctly supported, actor/thermal models are cleanly separated |
